# Cloudflare tunnel configuration — REFERENCE ONLY
#
# You don't copy or edit this file. `uis network init cloudflare` writes
# .uis.secrets/service-keys/cloudflare.env itself, with exactly the two
# variables below. This template documents what lands in it.
#
# Create the tunnel at: https://one.dash.cloudflare.com/ → Networks → Tunnels
#
# THERE IS NO KEY, CERTIFICATE OR API TOKEN TO CREATE FOR THIS FILE.
# UIS deploys Cloudflare's token-based connector. The tunnel token is a
# self-contained credential that embeds the tunnel id and its secret, so there
# is no `cloudflared tunnel login`, no cert.pem and no per-tunnel credentials
# file — that was the older certificate-based model, kept only under
# networking/cloudflare/legacy/. TLS terminates at Cloudflare's edge, so the
# cluster holds no certificate either.
#
# The DNS record and the tunnel itself are normally created by hand in the
# dashboard. If you instead use `uis network create cloudflare` to create them
# via the Cloudflare API, THAT step needs its own, separately-scoped API
# token — see cloudflare-api.env.template, a different file from this one.

# Tunnel token from the dashboard's install command (long string starting "ey").
# The ONLY credential the tunnel needs — read by 820-deploy and 822-verify.
CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=""

# Optional. The apex domain routed through the tunnel, e.g. example.com.
# Enables nothing but the end-to-end HTTPS probe in
# `uis network verify cloudflare`; leave empty to skip that one check.
BASE_DOMAIN_CLOUDFLARE=""

# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# MORE THAN ONE TUNNEL ON THIS INSTALLATION?
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# 'uis network init cloudflare --env <name>' writes a SEPARATE file instead
# of this one — cloudflare-<name>.env (lowercase), e.g. cloudflare-test.env,
# cloudflare-prod.env — and patches CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN_<NAME> /
# BASE_DOMAIN_CLOUDFLARE_<NAME> (uppercase <NAME>) instead of the bare keys
# above. This bare file and its keys are untouched by that path. Supported
# <name>/<NAME>: dev, test, prod — see provision-host/uis/lib/cloudflare-envs.sh.
